From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luke Craig <lacraig3@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 09:33:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] panda: block callbacks learn of a longjmp out of the block

A fault, an exception raised by a block's last instruction, or cpu_loop_exit_noexc leaves
the block by longjmp. With the block-exec callbacks run from the block's own code (TB
chaining on), the block a vCPU was running has to end there: after_block_exec, exited
early (TB_EXIT_REQUESTED), before the exception is delivered. Nothing pending, nothing
done: an empty inline without --enable-panda.

SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-or-later
Origin: new
---
 accel/tcg/cpu-exec.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/accel/tcg/cpu-exec.c b/accel/tcg/cpu-exec.c
index ef7a6027f290405544d93241c4a30ae0a803c56e..2c9570defa1090f734632d63cc98a40f9c47ee92 100644
--- a/accel/tcg/cpu-exec.c
+++ b/accel/tcg/cpu-exec.c
@@ -584,6 +584,8 @@ static void cpu_exec_longjmp_cleanup(CPUState *cpu)
         bql_unlock();
     }
     assert_no_pages_locked();
+    /* PANDA: the block this vCPU was running ends here (after_block_exec, exited early). */
+    panda_callbacks_block_longjmp(cpu);
 }
 
 void cpu_exec_step_atomic(CPUState *cpu)
